---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/aboutus.css";
---

<Layout>
  <section
    class="hero-welcome-section"
    style="padding: 60px 0; overflow-x: hidden;"
  >
    <div class="container">
      <div class="align-items-center row">
        <div class="col-lg-5 col-md-12">
          <div class="hero-content">
            <h1 class="hero-title">WELCOME TO <span>NAIVAIDYA,</span></h1>
            <h2 class="hero-subtitle">
              Where Health Feels Like <span>Home.</span>
            </h2>

            <p class="hero-description">
              An ISO 9001:2015 private medical clinic led by expert consultants
              offering consultation, diagnosis and treatment all in one place.
              From women&apos;s health and Medical care to personalized
              exercise, diet and nutrition plans, our integrated approach
              ensures accurate diagnosis, effective treatment, and long-term
              wellness. At Naivaidya, you're not just a patient - you&apos;re
              part of a community built on trust, empathy, and excellence.

              <span id="moreText" style="display: none;"
                >Experience healthcare where you feel cared for, supported, and
                empowered to live your best life.</span
              >
            </p>

            <div class="hero-buttons">
              <button id="readMoreBtn" class="theme-btn btn-green"
                >Read More</button
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="order-first order-lg-last col-lg-7 col-md-12">
          <div class="hero-image-container">
            <img
              src="https://res.cloudinary.com/daoju0r3c/image/upload/v1755375991/WhatsApp_Image_2025-07-24_at_15.23.21_1_tphyoj.jpg"
              alt="Naivaidya Healthcare Team"
              class="hero-image"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="department_listing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-12">
          <div class="department_list_inner">
            <div class="image">
              <img
                src="https://res.cloudinary.com/daoju0r3c/image/upload/c_crop,w_770,h_600,x_259,y_138/v1755410952/WhatsApp_Image_2025-07-24_at_15.23.16_1_r1hlaq.jpg"
                class="img-fluid"
                alt="Dr. Saurabh Jain"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="li_dp_content">
              <h2>Dr. Saurabh Jain</h2>
              <h4>
                Consultant Physician | MBBS, DNB (Medicine), PG Diabetology
                (Boston), PGD Endocrinology (RCP, UK)
              </h4>
              <p style="font-size: 13px;">
                With over 15 years of experience, Dr. Saurabh Jain specializes
                in Internal Medicine, with special interest in Diabetes and
                Cardiac care. He consults at Naivaidya Healthcare and is
                affiliated with Breach Candy, Sir HN Reliance Foundation,
                Jaslok, and Cumballa Hill Hospital. A former physician with the
                Indian Air Force and Railways, he holds advanced certifications
                from Boston University and RCP, UK. He is an active member of
                IMA, API, ASE, and the Jain Doctors Association, and regularly
                contributes to medical conferences and research. He has keen
                interest in traditional and non medicinal ways of healing and he
                blends conventional and scientific techniques in planning
                patient treatments. Active fitness enthusiast believes in
                practicing what he preaches. Avid runner participates in
                marathons, certified scuba diver.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-12">
          <div class="department_list_inner">
            <div class="image">
              <img
                src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dux0kv81i/image/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1781614130/amk99utnzzr2glpr8wqd.png"
                class="img-fluid"
                alt="Dr. Zimpu Mehta Jain"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="li_dp_content">
              <h2>Dr. Zimpu Mehta Jain</h2>
              <h4>
                Consulting Obstetrician & Gynaecologist | MBBS, DGO, FCPS, DNB
              </h4>
              <p style="font-size: 13px;">
                Dr Zimpu is a Compassionate gynecologist with 15 + years of
                experience in providing comprehensive women's health services,
                specializing in minimally invasive gynecological surgeries and
                high-risk pregnancies. She also specialises in other
                women&apos;s health issues, such as menopause, hormone problems,
                contraception (birth control), and infertility and also
                adolescent gynecological issues. She is affiliated with Breach
                Candy Hospital, Asian Cancer Institute and Cumballa Hill
                Hospital, St Elizabeth Hospital and Ruxmani Hospital. She has
                proven ability to build strong patient relationships and deliver
                positive health outcomes. She has completed her MBBS from K.J.
                Somaiya Medical College, followed by her Post graduate studies
                from Seth G.S. Medical College & K.E.M. Hospital, Mumbai. She
                has undergone specialized laparoscopic training under Dr. Hafeez
                Rehman at Sunrise Hospital, Kochi, and has worked in the
                Department of Oncology- Gynaecology at Tata Memorial Hospital.
                Dr. Jain is a life member of FOGSI, IAGE, and the Jain Doctors
                Federation and has received many awards and recognition for her
                outstanding performance and contribution to the field.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="../scripts/aboutus.js"></script>
</Layout>
